---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Accessibility, Prakash Upadhyay" description="A proposed CSS user preference for sudden HDR brightness spikes, filed with the W3C CSS Working Group." current="work" progress>
<section aria-labelledby="page-title" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line)">
<div style="position: relative; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px clamp(16px, 4vw, 40px) 88px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-weight: var(--weight-label)">
<a href="/work" style="color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: none">Work</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Accessibility</span>
</nav>
<h1 id="page-title" style="margin: 0; color: var(--display); font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 0.98">Accessibility</h1>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px); font-weight: 300; color: var(--text-muted)">Comfort. Standards. Defaults.</p>
<p style="margin: 0; max-width: 680px; font-size: 19px; text-wrap: pretty">Proposed a web standard so people can turn off sudden HDR brightness spikes, the way they can turn off motion.</p>
</div>
</section>

<main>
<section aria-label="Expertise, interests and learnings" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px clamp(16px, 4vw, 40px) 0">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 48px 40px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h2 class="section-title">Expertise</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 16px">
<li>Web accessibility: WCAG, user preference media queries, inclusive design</li>
<li>CSS standards</li>
<li>Color and HDR imaging</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h2 class="section-title">Interests</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 16px">
<li>Photosensitivity and visual comfort</li>
<li>Standards work</li>
<li>Accessible defaults</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h2 class="section-title">Learnings</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 16px">
<li>Accessibility bugs can be invisible to the tools we review with</li>
