<p style="margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-faint)">The bicycle rides down as you read, its wheels turning and its frame tilting with your scroll. It jumps without moving when reduced motion is on.</p>
</aside>

<article style="flex: 999 1 560px; min-width: 0; max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 72px">

<section id="moment" aria-labelledby="h-moment" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-moment" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">The moment</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; text-wrap: pretty">18 Oct 2026, a dim café. A LinkedIn job alert in Yahoo Mail on a MacBook Pro: one company logo glowed far brighter than anything else on screen. A screenshot of it looked completely normal.</p>
</section>

<section id="investigation" aria-labelledby="h-investigation" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-investigation" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">Investigation</h3>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<li>Read the JPEG's bytes: an Apple "BT.2100 PQ" ICC profile (CICP 9/16/0/1). The logo's white is PQ code 255, which means 10,000 nits, about 49x the 203 nit graphics white in ITU-R BT.2408.</li>
<li>Explained the screenshot puzzle: screenshots are tone-mapped to SDR, so the glow never appears in reviews or bug reports.</li>
<li>Found the gap: authors can cap HDR (<code>dynamic-range-limit</code>) and test for it (<code>@media (dynamic-range)</code>), and the spec says browsers "should" offer a user limit, but no user preference exists.</li>
<li>Measured adoption from Chrome Platform Status: <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> on 58.3% of page loads, <code>dynamic-range-limit</code> on 0.66%.</li>
<li>Borrowed a precedent from audio: loudness normalization (BS.1770, EBU R128, the US CALM Act, Spotify's levels).</li>
</ul>
<figure style="margin: 16px 0 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<img src="/images/hdr/brightness-dark.png" width="1640" height="776" alt="Bar chart of brightness in nits: graphics white 203, MacBook Pro XDR sustained 1,000, MacBook Pro XDR peak 1,600, and the logo file's white 10,000. The screen peak line clips the logo." style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-card-lg)">
<figcaption style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted)">The logo asks for 49x the brightness of graphics white. Illustration, not a screen capture.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

<section id="built" aria-labelledby="h-built" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-built" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">What I built</h3>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<li>An explainer in three reading levels: technical, balanced and plain language.</li>
<li>A live demo that recreates the inbox with the original logo file, with a toggle between today's behavior, a constrained cap and "if my preference were respected".</li>
<li>Evidence that works on any screen: a brightness chart, and phone photos (since screenshots can't show HDR), as an animation that falls back to a still image for people who prefer reduced motion.</li>
</ul>
<figure style="margin: 16px 0 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<picture>
<source srcset="/images/hdr/photo-comparison.jpg" media="(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)" />
<img src="/images/hdr/photo-blink.gif" alt="Phone photos of the demo inbox: the logo glowing far brighter than the page, then the same logo matching the page when the preference is respected." loading="lazy" style="display: block; width: 100%; max-height: 640px; object-fit: contain; background: var(--letterbox); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-card-lg)" />
</picture>
<figcaption style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted)">Phone photos of the demo, since screenshots can't show HDR. A still image replaces the animation when reduced motion is on.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

<section id="proposal" aria-labelledby="h-proposal" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-proposal" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">The proposal</h3>
<ol style="margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(280px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 16px">
<li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)">
<span style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: 300; color: var(--display); line-height: 1">01</span>
<span>A browser or OS override that caps HDR brightness and that pages can't undo.</span>
</li>
<li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)">
<span style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: 300; color: var(--display); line-height: 1">02</span>
<span>A media feature (<code>prefers-reduced-peak-brightness</code> or <code>prefers-dynamic-range</code>) so authors can adapt design, not just brightness.</span>
</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section id="outcome" aria-labelledby="h-outcome" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-outcome" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">Outcome so far</h3>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<li>Filed as <a href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14616" style="text-underline-offset: 4px">w3c/csswg-drafts#14616</a> on 18 Oct 2026, cross-linked from the existing discussion in #11790.</li>
<li>Shared on LinkedIn with a call for use cases.</li>
<li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic">[Update as it happens: CSSWG replies, browser tickets, use cases collected.]</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="learnings" aria-labelledby="h-learnings" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<h3 id="h-learnings" style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--display)">Learnings</h3>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<li>Accessibility bugs can be invisible to the tools we review with. Screenshots hid this one completely.</li>
<li>The harm is relative, not absolute: a spike against its surroundings, which is why dimming the whole screen doesn't help.</li>
<li>Standards move on evidence and use cases, so lead with a real case, numbers and a demo anyone can try.</li>
<li>Practice what you propose: the explainer's own animation respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</li>
</ul>
</section>

</article>
</div>
</main>
</Base>

<script>
  // The bicycle rides down the index as the page scrolls, between section stops, and its wheels
  // turn with the scroll (backwards when scrolling up). With reduced motion it jumps from stop to
  // stop and the wheels stay still. The bike pitches a little as it rides, as if over a real road;
  // the tilt comes from the scroll position, so it plays back the same way in reverse.
  const toc = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-toc]');
  if (toc) {
    const links = [...toc.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-toc-link]')];
    const bike = toc.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-toc-bike]');
    const wheels = [...toc.querySelectorAll<SVGGElement>('[data-toc-wheel]')];
    const progress = toc.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-toc-progress]');
    const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const ROW = 44;
    const targets = links
      .map((a) => document.getElementById(a.dataset.tocLink ?? ''))
      .filter((el): el is HTMLElement => !!el);
    const update = () => {
      const line = window.innerHeight * 0.35;
      const tops = targets.map((el) => el.getBoundingClientRect().top);
      let index = 0;
      tops.forEach((t, i) => {
        if (t <= line) index = i;
      });
      // How far between this stop and the next, from 0 to 1
      const next = tops[index + 1];
      const span = next === undefined ? 1 : next - tops[index];
      const along = reduced || next === undefined ? 0 : Math.min(Math.max((line - tops[index]) / span, 0), 1);
      const pos = (index + along) * ROW;
      links.forEach((a, i) => {
        if (i === index) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location');
        else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
        a.dataset.state = i < index ? 'done' : '';
      });
      if (bike) {
        const y = window.scrollY;
        const tilt = reduced ? 0 : Math.sin(y * 0.018) * 3 + Math.sin(y * 0.047) * 1.5;
        bike.style.transform = `translateY(${pos}px) rotate(${tilt}deg)`;
      }
      if (progress) progress.style.height = `${pos}px`;
      if (!reduced) wheels.forEach((w) => (w.style.transform = `rotate(${window.scrollY * 0.8}deg)`));
    };
    let queued = false;
    window.addEventListener(
      'scroll',
      () => {
        if (queued) return;
        queued = true;
        requestAnimationFrame(() => {
          queued = false;
          update();
        });
      },
      { passive: true },
    );
    window.addEventListener('resize', update);
    update();
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* The index stays in view beside the article on wide screens */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .toc-aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 110px;
    }
  }

  .toc {
    position: relative;
  }

  .toc__track {
    position: absolute;
    left: 11px;
    top: 22px;
    bottom: 22px;
    border-left: 1.5px dashed var(--outline);
  }

  .toc__progress {
    position: absolute;
    left: 11px;
    top: 22px;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 1.5px solid var(--text);
  }

  /* Sits on the current stop and rides down the dashed track */
  .toc__bike {
    transform-origin: 50% 80%;
    position: absolute;
    left: -9px;
    top: 0;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--ink);
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .toc__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .toc__link {
    height: var(--touch-target);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .toc__link[data-state='done'] {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .toc__link[aria-current='location'] {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .toc__node {
    width: 24px;
    flex: 0 0 24px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .toc__node::before {
    content: '';
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border-radius: var(--radius-circle);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--control-border);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .toc__link[data-state='done'] .toc__node::before {
    background: var(--text-muted);
    border-color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .toc__link[aria-current='location'] .toc__node::before {
    opacity: 0;
  }
</style>
